# PLACEHOLDER — a stalk that has been soaked until the bark lets go of the core.
#
# The matrix traces Warlon Mhite's hand-drawn item/hemp_stem.png pixel for pixel: it is the
# same stalk, only retted, so the two have to read as the same object at 16px. Only the
# palette moves. If hemp_stem.png is ever redrawn, re-trace this from it
# (`mctex.py extract .../hemp_stem.png`) rather than leaving the two shapes to drift.
#
# The palette is the one thing retting actually does to a stalk that you can see: the green
# goes and the bark greys off to a drab straw-tan as the pectin rots out. Same luminance
# structure as the original ramp, so the shading Warlon drew still lands.

@palette retted
. = none
1 = 3A3325
2 = 6B5F42
3 = 998A63
4 = C3B78E
5 = DED5B8

@texture item/retted_hemp_stem 16x16 type=item palette=retted
